/n# Request Refund

## OpenAPI Specification

```yaml
openapi: 3.0.1
info:
  title: ''
  description: ''
  version: 1.0.0
paths:
  /{ProviderUrl}/refund:
    post:
      summary: Request Refund
      deprecated: false
      description: >-
        When a refund is requested from a customer the following request will be
        sent to the payment provider from Zid Payments. After processing the
        refund, we expect refund Id and refund reference to be returned back in
        the response. Also, a webhook shall be sent to notify Zid Payments with
        success or failure result.  
      tags:
        - Default module/Payment API/Refund
      parameters:
        - name: ProviderUrl
          in: path
          description: >-
            The base URL of the payment provider’s API. ZidPay will use this URL
            to send requests such as token generation, payment execution,
            refunds, and Apple Pay registration. This should point to the root
            domain or environment-specific endpoint provided by the payment
            provider.
          required: true
          example: https://api.paymentprovider.com
          schema:
            type: string
        - name: Authorization
          in: header
          description: >-
            All secured endpoints require an Authorization header using Basic
            Authentication. The value should be the secret key provided by the
            payment provider during merchant onboarding.
          required: true
          example: 'Authorization: Basic secret_key'
          schema:
            type: string
      requestBody:
        content:
          application/json:
            schema:
              type: object
              title: RefundRequestDto
              description: >-
                Request body for initiating a refund from ZidPay to the payment
                provider.
              properties:
                paymentId:
